# Ephemeral state the hooks read/write at runtime; never commit.
.claude/.evidence-reads
AGENT_STOP
STEER.md

# Nothing else is ignored, on purpose. Everything a run produces -- LEVELS.md,
# EVIDENCE.md, RUBRIC.md, SCOREBOARD.json, PROGRESS.md, PAUSED_ACTIONS.md,
# memory/, evidence/, logs/ -- is committed by the wrapper each cycle, because
# `git log` being a real record of what the loop did is part of the handoff, not
# an accident. Your clone accumulates its own task history; that is the design.
#
# The template repo simply ships with none of those files present, so a fresh
# clone starts clean.
